{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:10Z","thinking":"**Investigating Graph Properties**\n\nThe primary question is whether any graph exists where the total domination number exceeds the Roman domination number. A direct search is required. Considering a specific search strategy, creating a script appears the most effective approach. The scope of the script expands to include a wider variety of graph classes for broader verification. Focusing on 10, a fast check is desired.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\nimport random\n\ndef fast_check(G):\n    # nodes are 0..n-1\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\n    adj = [list(G.neighbors(i)) for i in range(n)]\n    if any(len(adj[i]) == 0 for i in range(n)):\n        return True # not applicable\n    \n    # Check if gamma_t <= 2: if any edge (u, v) has N(u) U N(v) == V\n    # If so, gamma_t <= 2 <= gamma_R (since gamma_R >= 2 for nontrivial)\n    for u, v in G.edges():\n        # check if N(u) U N(v) covers all nodes\n        # a node w is covered if w in adj[u] or w in adj[v]\n        # (note: u is in adj[v] and v is in adj[u], so u and v are covered)\n        covered = set(adj[u]) | set(adj[v])\n        if len(covered) == n:\n            return True # gamma_t <= 2, so gamma_t <= gamma_R always\n    \n    # Compute exact gamma_t\n    gamma_t = None\n    adj_sets = [set(adj[i]) for i in range(n)]\n    for k in range(3, n + 1):\n        for S in itertools.combinations(range(n), k):\n            S_set = set(S)\n            if all(adj_sets[i] & S_set for i in range(n)):\n                gamma_t = k\n                break\n        if gamma_t is not None:\n            break\n    if gamma_t is None:\n        gamma_t = n\n\n    # Now compute gamma_R:\n    # Does there exist a Roman dominating function of weight < gamma_t?\n    # Test weights W from 2 to gamma_t - 1:\n    for W in range(2, gamma_t):\n        for k2 in range(0, W // 2 + 1):\n            k1 = W - 2 * k2\n            for V2 in itertools.combinations(range(n), k2):\n                V2_set = set(V2)\n                dom = set()\n                for u in V2:\n                    dom.update(adj[u])\n                # uncovered 0-nodes: nodes not in V2 and not in dom\n                uncovered = set(range(n)) - V2_set - dom\n                if len(uncovered) <= k1:\n                    # Valid Roman dominating function of weight W < gamma_t!\n                    print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE! n={n}, edges={list(G.edges())}, gamma_t={gamma_t}, gamma_R<={W}\")\n                    return False\n    return True\n\nprint(\"Running fast check on random graphs...\")\ncount = 0\nfor n in range(4, 11):\n    for trial in range(5000):\n        p = random.uniform(0.1, 0.9)\n        G = nx.erdos_renyi_graph(n, p)\n        if not fast_check(G):\n            exit(0)\n        count += 1\nprint(f\"Checked {count} random graphs. All satisfied gamma_t <= gamma_R!\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Running fast check on 35,000 random graphs","toolSummary":"Check random graphs"}}]}
