{"step_index":121,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:30Z","thinking":"**Hypothesizing a general relationship**\n\nExamining multiple cases shows $\\gamma_t \\le \\gamma_R$. Noticing that, for all examples observed, this inequality holds. Questioning whether this is always the case. Considering the possibility of a graph where $\\gamma_t > \\gamma_R$. Deciding to test if a counterexample exists among connected graphs of order 8.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport random\n\n# Let us check 20,000 graphs of orders 8 to 16\nfor trial in range(20000):\n    n = random.randint(8, 16)\n    # try various types: tree, erdos-renyi, regular, bipartite, barbell, etc.\n    choice = random.randint(0, 5)\n    if choice == 0:\n        G = nx.erdos_renyi_graph(n, random.uniform(0.1, 0.4))\n    elif choice == 1:\n        G = nx.random_regular_graph(random.randint(2, min(5, n-1)), n) if (n * min(3, n-1)) % 2 == 0 else nx.path_graph(n)\n    elif choice == 2:\n        G = nx.bipartite.random_graph(n // 2, n - n // 2, random.uniform(0.2, 0.6))\n    elif choice == 3:\n        G = nx.barabasi_albert_graph(n, random.randint(1, 3))\n    elif choice == 4:\n        G = nx.powerlaw_cluster_graph(n, random.randint(1, 3), 0.5)\n    else:\n        G = nx.watts_strogatz_graph(n, 4, 0.3)\n    \n    # ensure no isolated vertices\n    if any(d == 0 for _, d in G.degree()):\n        continue\n    \n    # We can check with ILP if gt > gr\n    # Using the fast ILP\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    adj = {u: set(G.neighbors(u)) for u in nodes}\n    \n    # Fast check if gamma_t <= 2\n    if any(len(adj[u] | adj[v]) == n for u, v in G.edges()):\n        continue\n    \n    import scipy.optimize\n    import numpy as np\n    \n    # ILP gamma_t\n    c_t = np.ones(n)\n    A_t = [[1 if v in adj[u] else 0 for v in nodes] for u in nodes]\n    res_t = scipy.optimize.milp(c=c_t, constraints=scipy.optimize.LinearConstraint(A_t, 1, np.inf),\n                                integrality=np.ones(n), bounds=scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1))\n    gt = int(round(res_t.fun))\n    \n    # If gt <= 2: continue\n    if gt <= 2:\n        continue\n    \n    # ILP gamma_R\n    c_R = np.array([1]*n + [2]*n)\n    A_R = []\n    b_l = []\n    for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\n        row[i] = 1\n        row[n + i] = 1\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            row[n + nodes.index(v)] = 1\n        A_R.append(row)\n        b_l.append(1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\n        row[i] = 1\n        row[n + i] = 1\n        A_R.append(row)\n        b_l.append(0)\n    \n    b_u = [np.inf]*n + [1]*n\n    res_R = scipy.optimize.milp(c=c_R, constraints=scipy.optimize.LinearConstraint(A_R, b_l, b_u),\n                                integrality=np.ones(2*n), bounds=scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1))\n    gr = int(round(res_R.fun))\n    \n    if gt > gr:\n        print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE FOUND! n={n}, edges={list(G.edges())}, gt={gt}, gr={gr}\")\n        exit(0)\n\nprint(\"Checked 20,000 diverse graphs! All satisfied gt <= gr!\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing 20,000 diverse graphs","toolSummary":"Test 20,000 diverse graphs"}}]}
